# HTTP headers applied to every route served from this origin.
# Netlify and any Netlify-compatible CDN (Cloudflare Pages, etc.) honour this file.
# The Vite dev server picks up the equivalent config from vite.config.ts.
#
# =============================================================================
# CONTENT SECURITY POLICY (CSP)
# =============================================================================
# This strict CSP protects smile4money against XSS and data exfiltration attacks.
# All resources must be from the same origin or explicitly whitelisted endpoints.
#
# DIRECTIVES RATIONALE:
#
# default-src 'self'
#   - Failsafe: any resource type not explicitly allowed defaults to same-origin only
#   - Blocks CDN resources, inline code, and cross-origin API calls
#   - Narrow exceptions are defined below for specific resource types
#
# script-src 'self'
#   - CRITICAL: only scripts from the same origin; disables inline scripts and eval
#   - Prevents XSS that could:
#     * Steal the user's private key or transaction signing credentials
#     * Inject malicious smart contract calls (e.g., sending funds to an attacker)
#     * Redirect the user to a phishing site
#   - Vite bundles all application code into these same-origin scripts
#   - No external JavaScript libraries are loaded from CDNs
#
# style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
#   - Tailwind CSS is configured for runtime JIT, inlining critical styles into the HTML
#   - Once the project migrates to static CSS generation, 'unsafe-inline' should be removed
#     and replaced with style hashes or 'strict-dynamic'
#   - Current approach: inline Tailwind CSS is necessary for the chosen build process
#
# connect-src 'self' <Stellar RPC endpoints>
#   - Restricts all XHR, fetch, WebSocket, and EventSource calls
#   - Only the same origin and official Stellar RPC endpoints are whitelisted:
#     * soroban-testnet.stellar.org  (Stellar Soroban testnet RPC)
#     * soroban-mainnet.stellar.org  (Stellar Soroban mainnet RPC)
#     * horizon-testnet.stellar.org  (Stellar Horizon testnet API)
#     * horizon.stellar.org          (Stellar Horizon mainnet API)
#   - Prevents exfiltration of user data, private keys, or signed transactions to untrusted APIs
#
# img-src 'self' data:
#   - Allows images from the same origin (e.g., /favicon.svg, /og-image.svg)
#   - Allows data: URIs for inlined SVG (e.g., base64-encoded favicons)
#   - No external image CDNs; all images are bundled
#
# font-src 'self'
#   - Only web fonts from the same origin
#   - No Google Fonts, Typekit, or other external font services
#
# media-src 'self'
#   - Restricts audio and video to the same origin
#
# object-src 'none'
#   - Disables <embed>, <object>, <applet>, and related tags entirely
#   - Eliminates Flash-based attacks and legacy plugin vulnerabilities
#
# base-uri 'self'
#   - Prevents <base> tag injection, ensuring relative URLs use the correct origin
#
# frame-ancestors 'none'
#   - Clickjacking protection: denies the application from being embedded in an <iframe>
#   - Even if an attacker tricks the user into visiting a malicious site, the app cannot be framed
#
# form-action 'self'
#   - Form submissions (POST) must target the same origin
#   - Prevents CSRF attacks that would submit forms to attacker-controlled servers
#
# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION UPGRADE PATH:
# =============================================================================
# As the build process evolves, consider these enhancements:
#
# 1. Replace 'unsafe-inline' in style-src with content-hash once Tailwind supports
#    static CSS generation:
#      style-src 'sha256-<tailwind-hash>'
#
# 2. Add script hashes if static script bundling is enabled:
#      script-src 'sha256-<main.js-hash>' 'sha256-<chunk.js-hash>'
#    Run: npm run build && npx lighthouse --output=json <url> | grep CSP
#
# 3. Consider report-uri or report-to for CSP violation monitoring in production:
#      report-uri https://smile4money.app/csp-report
#      report-to csp-endpoint
#
# 4. Monitor Google CSP Evaluator recommendations quarterly:
#      https://csp-evaluator.withgoogle.com/
#
# =============================================================================
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org https://soroban-mainnet.stellar.org https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org https://horizon.stellar.org; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), battery=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
